<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bhuvanaikabahu IV</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1341–1351</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bhuvanaikabahu IV was a Sinhalese king who moved the royal seat from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurunegala">Kurunegala</a> to Gampola on the Mahaweli river around 1341. His reign saw the building of the Gadaladeniya and Lankatilaka temples, which blend Sinhalese, South Indian and other styles. Royal power was weak, and ministers of the Alakeshvara family steadily gained influence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bhuvanaikabahu-iv.jpg" alt="Bhuvanaikabahu IV" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cherubino · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gadaladeniya_Viharaya_20.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
